# Colima writes its own host entry here; ssh ignores this line if the file is absent
Include ~/.colima/ssh_config

# Ghostty terminfo fallback for remote hosts
Host *
    SetEnv TERM=xterm-256color

Host github.com
    HostName github.com
    User git
    IdentityFile ~/.ssh/git-id_ed25519
    AddKeysToAgent yes
    UseKeychain yes

Host otto
    HostName 100.111.32.113
    User io
    Port 22

Host zero
    HostName zero.hyrax-boga.ts.net
    User lacy
    IdentityFile ~/.ssh/git-id_ed25519

# fleet-health (moved to graphite 2026-09-24): library over LAN and Tailscale.
# fleet-health-check.sh dials these two IPs and never types the `library` alias, so
# the `Host library` block below does not cover it.
#
# Counted in fleet-health 03da7c7, fleet-health-check.sh blob b145fb38. The two IP
# literals appear 22 times, but 22 is a grep count and not a call-site count: it is
# 13 real ssh/rsync invocations, 1 curl (tdarr 3626, no credential) and 8 prose or
# CHECK_DETAIL mentions. Of the 13, THREE pass `-i fleet_health_ed25519` themselves
# (the rsync push's `-e` at 3409, that push's prune at 3413, the bas-nas probe at
# 3558) and TEN do not. SSH_OPTS at line 234 carries no -i, so those ten resolve
# their credential right here. Do not write 22; the number that depends on this
# block is ten on graphite.
#
# On zero it is all 13. fleet_health_ed25519 does not exist there, and a
# command-line `-i` naming a missing file neither pins nor fails: it warns and falls
# through to the remaining identities. So zero's three -i sites also land on the
# second IdentityFile line below. Measured 2026-10-28 from zero, and the same
# mechanism re-proved from graphite: `-i <nonexistent>` against root@100.119.64.141
# gives rc 0 as root with only `Warning: Identity file ... not accessible`, while a
# real throwaway ed25519 is the control at rc 255 publickey.
#
# Two IdentityFile lines, same rule as `Host library` and for the same reason
# (LACA-2770). A config IdentityFile REPLACES ssh's five built-in default identities,
# `IdentitiesOnly no` does NOT bring them back, and `IdentitiesOnly yes` additionally
# kills the command-line `-i` escape, so it must not appear here. This file is a
# synced dotfile: on zero `~/.ssh` is a symlink into the dotfiles tree, so a pull
# rewrites these lines verbatim. fleet_health_ed25519 exists only on graphite and
# zero's authorized key at library is ~/.ssh/id_ed25519, so the single-line form
# would leave zero offering one nonexistent key and nothing else. Order matters:
# fleet_health stays FIRST so graphite still tries the intended credential first,
# and a listed key that is missing costs only a warning. Measured 2026-10-27, i.e.
# BEFORE this block landed on main: graphite rc 0 through these lines; zero rc 0 on
# its built-in defaults, because zero's checked-out config then carried neither this
# block nor the one below.
Host 192.168.1.161 100.119.64.141
  User root
  IdentityFile ~/.ssh/fleet_health_ed25519
  # Expected missing on graphite; do NOT delete it as dead. This is zero's real
  # library credential, proven from zero 2026-10-27 with `ssh -o IdentitiesOnly=yes
  # -i ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 root@library.hyrax-boga.ts.net` authenticating as root.
  # Dropping it costs zero library access on the next sync (LAC-5893, LACA-2771).
  IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519

# Same host by its MagicDNS alias. ssh matches Host on the name you TYPE, not the
# resolved IP, so the block above never fires for `ssh library` or the fleet-health
# git remote (ssh://root@library/...). Without this, every caller that does not
# pass -i fleet_health_ed25519 itself gets rc 128 publickey (LACA-2768, LAC-5893).
#
# BOTH IdentityFile lines are load-bearing, and with both present this file is SAFE
# to sync: fleet_health_ed25519 carries graphite, id_ed25519 carries zero. The second
# line is the only thing that makes a dotfiles-tracked library block syncable to a
# host whose library access runs on a default key. A config IdentityFile REPLACES
# ssh's five built-in default identities, and `IdentitiesOnly no` does NOT bring them
# back. This file is a synced dotfile and the fleet-health key exists only on
# graphite, so on zero a lone first line would suppress ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 (zero's
# authorized key) and cost it library access. Listing the fallback explicitly keeps a
# missing key to a warning. The sync is not hypothetical: on zero `~/.ssh` is a
# symlink to dotfiles/home/.ssh and `~/.ssh/config` is the SAME INODE as the tracked
# file (270695901, verified 2026-10-27), so a pull rewrites what ssh reads at once.
# Measured 2026-10-27: graphite rc 0 THROUGH this block; zero rc 0 WITHOUT it, on its
# built-in defaults, because zero's checked-out config has no library block yet. That
# is why the single-IdentityFile form is specifically dangerous for zero: it would
# replace working defaults with one filename that does not exist there.
# `IdentitiesOnly yes` is also wrong here, for
# the same reason. Command-line `-i` does NOT behave this way (it keeps the
# defaults), which is why evidence from an `-i` run does not transfer to this block.
#
# Side effect, read this before writing a probe (LACA-2769, LAC-5949). With this block
# live a BARE `ssh library` or `git fetch library` SUCCEEDS on graphite, so "the bare
# probe is refused" has stopped being a host tell; a green bare probe means this
# config, not an authorized default key. Through the ALIAS, `-o IdentitiesOnly=yes
# -i <throwaway>` does NOT get you back the refusal: IdentitiesOnly drops agent keys,
# not the IdentityFile lines below. Nor does `env HOME=<elsewhere>`, because ssh takes
# the user config path from the passwd entry and ignores $HOME.
#
# To see the refusal you need BOTH halves, and which half does the work depends on
# how you address the host:
#   1. ESCAPE the target's config IdentityFile: address a name that no `Host` pattern
#      in this file matches (the FQDN root@library.hyrax-boga.ts.net; `Host *` sets
#      no identity), OR pass `-F /dev/null`. An IP is NOT a substitute, because the
#      block above matches both of library's IPs, so an IP still fires a block.
#   2. SUPPRESS ssh's five built-in defaults, with `-o IdentitiesOnly=yes` plus an
#      `-i <file that EXISTS>` (a fresh throwaway ed25519). A missing `-i` file only
#      warns and falls through, so it pins nothing.
# For the FQDN, half 1 comes free with the name, so only half 2 moves the rc there.
# That is the one case where `-F /dev/null` is redundant. Do NOT carry "`-F` does
# nothing" as a general rule: through an ALIAS it is the whole discriminator.
#
# FQDN matrix, measured 2026-10-27 on BOTH hosts against
# root@library.hyrax-boga.ts.net, BatchMode=yes and SSH_AUTH_SOCK cleared:
#   arm                                          graphite   zero
#   FQDN bare                                       255        0
#   FQDN + -F /dev/null                             255        0
#   FQDN + -o IdentitiesOnly=yes -i <throwaway>     255      255
#   FQDN + both of the above                        255      255
# ALIAS matrix, measured from zero 2026-10-27 and again 2026-10-28 against the
# `graphite` alias at the end of this file (IdentityFile + IdentitiesOnly yes):
#   alias bare (control)                             0
#   alias + -o IdentitiesOnly=yes -i <throwaway>     0   authed on the CONFIG key
#   alias + -F /dev/null + the same pin            255   publickey
#   raw IP + the same pin                          255   publickey
#
# So `-F /dev/null` moves no rc in the FQDN matrix and is decisive in the alias one.
# The bare FQDN reads 255 on graphite only by accident: graphite has no authorized
# default key at library, zero's ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 is authorized. The one
# host-independent refusal probe is the FQDN PLUS `-o IdentitiesOnly=yes -i <fresh
# throwaway ed25519>`; carry that form. zero's bare rc 0 above is the explicit
# root@FQDN form, and is also a free re-proof of the second IdentityFile line below.
# The bare ALIAS behaves differently there: `ssh library` on zero is 255 today
# (`lacy@library: Permission denied`; with no block, User falls back to lacy, not
# root) and 0 under this file, so landing it REPAIRS zero's `ssh library` and its
# `library` git remote rather than merely not breaking them. The other tell that
# still works is whether ~/.ssh/fleet_health_ed25519 exists.
Host library
  User root
  IdentityFile ~/.ssh/fleet_health_ed25519
  # Expected missing on graphite; do NOT delete it as dead. This is zero's real
  # library credential, proven from zero 2026-10-27 with `ssh -o IdentitiesOnly=yes
  # -i ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 root@library.hyrax-boga.ts.net` authenticating as root.
  # Dropping it costs zero library access on the next sync (LAC-5893, LACA-2771).
  IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519

# Coolify OLD, every buildandserve prod service (LACA-1912).
# Key copied from zero 2026-10-21, same identity as zero's ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
# (both SHA256:RF9pvVcI6QOEr6mGVYRBIqvpzmt7YD1zrzjYv4SOuhI).
#
# Same shape as the two library blocks (LACA-2770), and the shared identity is NOT
# what saves it: what ssh resolves is the FILENAME, and `zero_id_ed25519` is a
# graphite-only filename. zero holds that same key as plain `id_ed25519`. With
# `IdentitiesOnly yes` and one path that does not exist there, this block was
# measured on zero at rc 255 publickey against a reachable host, so listing the
# fallback is load-bearing here too. Measured 2026-10-27: zero as-written rc 255,
# zero with the second line rc 0, graphite rc 0 still on zero_id_ed25519.
Host coolify-old 178.156.130.157
  HostName 178.156.130.157
  User root
  IdentityFile ~/.ssh/zero_id_ed25519
  IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519

# zero's lane to graphite (main e7d33f7). LOAD-BEARING FOR zero, DO NOT DELETE, and
# do not "fix" it to match the two-IdentityFile rule above without measuring first.
# paperclip_graphite_ed25519 is the only key graphite accepts from zero and this is
# the only block that names it. Measured from zero 2026-10-28 through the raw IP so
# no Host block matches, BatchMode=yes, SSH_AUTH_SOCK cleared: bare rc 255 publickey,
# `-o IdentitiesOnly=yes -i ~/.ssh/id_ed25519` rc 255, `-i paperclip_graphite_ed25519`
# rc 0 AUTHED_AS=lacy. Dropping this block costs zero the bridge lane, the
# day-inputs scp, fleet-health-check.sh's graphite probes, paperclip-upgrade-check.sh
# and test/deploy/lac5910-install-marker-test.sh, all silently (LACA-2774).
#
# The `IdentitiesOnly yes` here is the shape the library blocks above forbid, and it
# is left alone deliberately. On graphite the named key does not exist, so this block
# would hard-fail rather than warn. It is inert instead: nothing on graphite types
# `graphite` as an ssh target (grepped across ~/.openclaw, ~/.paperclip/scripts and
# ~/repo/fleet-health 2026-10-28; every hit is prose or a zero-side caller), and
# graphite self-ssh measured rc 255 both with and without this block. Change it only
# with a zero-side measurement in hand, because zero is the host it serves.
Host graphite
    HostName 100.78.6.88
    User lacy
    IdentityFile ~/.ssh/paperclip_graphite_ed25519
    IdentitiesOnly yes
